  "id": "Compound::DB01403 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Methotrimeprazine is shown to bind to Chrm4 and to participate in G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity, which is also associated with Chrm2. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Methotrimeprazine may influence Chrm2 through the activation of G-protein coupled receptors. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Methotrimeprazine interacts with Chrm4, which in turn is involved in the activation of G-protein coupled receptors, ultimately leading to the participation of Chrm2 in these activities. The overlapping pathways suggest that Methotrimeprazine may modulate Chrm2 through a common receptor-mediated mechanism, possibly involving acetylcholine signaling. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Methotrimeprazine and Chrm2, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Chrm2 in this context.",
